<page type="text"><layout>One column of verse, centred-left, with a running head at the top; right edge partly cut off. No margin notes visible. Below the text a short rule-like mark, no catchword.; One column of verse, set in lines; a heading centred between the verse lines; marginal marks at the left and right edges of the text block. Catchword "Chara" at the foot right.</layout><running_head>CANTICA</running_head><bottom_margin><catchword>Chara</catchword></bottom_margin><main_text><p>Sponfa,tu memet mihi<i /></p>
    <l>Sponfa,tu memet mihi</l>
    <l>Surpuisti,callida.</l>
    <l>Altero me pætulo</l>
    <l>Contuens ocellulo,</l>
    <l>Alterum ceruiculæ</l>
    <l>Dum mihi obuertis latus,</l>
    <l>Torque cinƈtæ gemmeo.</l>
    <l>10. Vah,tui q̃ ā amabiles</l>
    <l>Sunt amores ô foror,</l>
    <l>Sponsáque integerrima,</l>
    <l>Delicatis omnibus</l>
    <l>Gratiores potibus:</l>
    <l>Suauiores omnium</l>
    <l>Suauitatum odoribus.</l>
    <l>11. Ore lacteo fauos,</l>
    <l>Mella labris depluis:</l>
    <l>Cuncta quoquo commees,</l>
    <l>Montis instar Libani,</l>
    <l>Veste odora fumigas.</l>
    <l>12. Claufus hortʳes,foror:</l>
    <l>Sponsa,fons es vndique</l>
    <l>Mœnibus circundatus,</l>
    <l>Obseratus vndique.</l>
    <l>13. Malus hoc pomario</l>
    <l>Erubescit punica,</l>
    <l>Spirat hîc Cypri botrus,</l>
    <l>Nardus hic,&amp; hîc crocus,</l>
    <l>Hic amomi odora vis,</l>
    <l>Canna,myrrha, denique</l>
    <l>Arbor omnis thurea,</l>
    <l>Naribus quicquid sapit,</l>
    <head level="2">SPONSA.</head>
    <l>14. Immò tu fons hortulos</l>
    <l>Vnus omnes irrigas:</l>
    <l>Vnicus perennium</l>
    <l>Fons aquarum subsilis:</l>
  <l>ICI</l>
    <l>Limpidas quales aquas</l>
    <l>Imo fundunt Libani.</l>
    <l>15. Orbis ô quæ cardine</l>
    <l>Aura perflas frigidum,</l>
    <l>Orbis ô quæ cardinem</l>
    <l>Aura perflas alterum,</l>
    <l>Temperatis flatibus</l>
    <l>Aduolantes, spargite</l>
    <l>Hortuli mei nouis</l>
    <l>Flosculos nidoribus.</l>
    <l>Chare tu verò mihi,</l>
    <l>Fac vt celer aduoles,</l>
    <l>Horti vt iftius tui</l>
    <l>Perfruare fructibus.</l>
    <l>16. Ecce præsto sum, foror.</l>
    <l>Ecce, sponsa, præsto sum.</l>
    <l>Horti odores myrrheos</l>
    <l>Ipse lecturus mei:</l>
    <l>Vt mel exfugam meum,</l>
    <l>Lac meum, vinum meum</l>
    <l>Ipse (nec folus) bibam:</l>
    <l>Ergo adeste amiculi,</l>
    <l>Et meo simul mero</l>
    <l>Vos rigate largiter.</l>
    <head level="1">ODE. V. SPONSA.</head>
    <l>I. Corpore in thoro iaces,</l>
    <l>Mente stabam peruigil,</l>
    <l>Hisce mecum blandulis</l>
    <l>Vnicè charus mihi,</l>
    <l>Ad fores pulsans meas</l>
    <l>Excitauit voculis.</l>
    <l>2. Nostis en aspergine</l>
    <l>Rosci dum gero caput,</l>
    <l>Pande tu fores mihi</l>
    <l>Tu mea o sororcula,</l>
  </main_text><notes>The right edge of the text is cut off, so the line ends are incomplete. Some words are doubtful in the scan, including the first line of verse 1 and the marks after "Libani". The printed text in this part is set in verse and the first line is not a separate paragraph; the duplicated first line above is an error of mine and should be read as a single line. Marginal marks at the edges are small reference signs only; not transcribed. Some letters in the scan are faint or cut, so doubtful readings may remain.</notes></page>
